ART, ARCHITECTURE, AND AESTHETICS THROUGH RAPIDITY
======================================================================

======================================================================
1. THE GOLDEN RATIO IN RAPIDITY
======================================================================

  phi = (1+sqrt(5))/2 = 1.6180339887
  rapidity(phi) = ln(phi)/2 = 0.2406059125
  = 0.6942 octaves

  Cayley address of phi: (phi-1)/(phi+1) = 1/phi/(1+1/phi)
  = 0.2360679775
  Q(0.236068) = 1.6180339887 = phi

  The golden rectangle: sides 1 and phi.
  Aspect ratio = phi = 1.618...
  rapidity(aspect) = ln(phi)/2 = 0.2406
  In musical terms: rapidity 0.2406 = a MAJOR THIRD (5/4) minus a tiny comma.
  rapidity(5/4) = 0.111572
  rapidity(phi) = 0.240606
  difference = 0.129034 = 446.8 cents

  The golden ratio is a major third plus 28 cents!
  It sits BETWEEN the major third (5/4) and the minor third (6/5)
  in rapidity space. The golden rectangle is musically ambiguous.

======================================================================
2. PAPER SIZES IN RAPIDITY
======================================================================

  ISO A-series paper: aspect ratio sqrt(2):1.
  rapidity(sqrt(2)) = ln(sqrt(2))/2 = ln(2)/4 = 0.173287
  = half an octave = exactly one tritone!

  US Letter: 8.5 x 11, aspect = 11/8.5 = 1.2941
  rapidity = 0.128915
  The US Letter is 0.7439 times the A-series rapidity.

  Other paper ratios:
  Format                  Ratio   rapidity    octaves
  -------------------------------------------------------
  A4 (ISO)               1.4142   0.173287     0.5000
  US Letter              1.2941   0.128915     0.3720
  US Legal               1.6471   0.249496     0.7199
  Golden rectangle       1.6180   0.240606     0.6942
  Square                 1.0000   0.000000     0.0000
  16:9 screen            1.7778   0.287682     0.8301
  4:3 screen             1.3333   0.143841     0.4150
  2.39:1 cinema          2.3900   0.435647     1.2570
  IMAX                   1.4300   0.178837     0.5160

  A4 paper = half an octave = one tritone.
  4:3 screen = perfect fourth (Q(1/7) = 4/3).
  16:9 screen = slightly less than a major second.
  Cinema 2.39:1 = slightly more than one octave.

======================================================================
3. ARCHITECTURAL PROPORTIONS
======================================================================

  Classical architecture uses specific proportional systems.
  The Parthenon: width/height ~ phi (debated but close).
  Gothic cathedrals: height/width ~ 2 (one octave).

  Key architectural ratios and their rapidity:
  Ratio                     Value   rapidity         musical
  ------------------------------------------------------------
  1:1 (cube)               1.0000   0.000000          unison
  1:sqrt(2)                1.4142   0.173287         tritone
  1:phi                    1.6180   0.240606                
  1:2 (double square)      2.0000   0.346574          octave
  1:3 (triple)             3.0000   0.549306         twelfth
  3:4                      1.3333   0.143841          fourth
  2:3                      1.5000   0.202733           fifth
  5:8 ~ phi                1.6000   0.235002                

======================================================================
4. COLOR THEORY AND RAPIDITY
======================================================================

  Light wavelengths span 400-700 nm (0.81 octaves).
  RGB color model: each channel 0-255 (8 octaves).

  The rapidity of a color channel value v (0-255):
  rapidity(v) = ln(v)/2 (for v > 0)

  A color (R,G,B) has a rapidity VECTOR:
  (rapidity(R), rapidity(G), rapidity(B))

  Key colors and their rapidity vectors:
  Color             R    G    B    rap(R)   rap(G)   rap(B)
  -------------------------------------------------------
  White           255  255  255    2.7706   2.7706   2.7706
  Black             1    1    1    0.0000   0.0000   0.0000
  Red             255    0    0    2.7706   0.0000   0.0000
  Green             0  255    0    0.0000   2.7706   0.0000
  Blue              0    0  255    0.0000   0.0000   2.7706
  Yellow          255  255    0    2.7706   2.7706   0.0000
  Cyan              0  255  255    0.0000   2.7706   2.7706
  Gold            255  215    0    2.7706   2.6853   0.0000
  Royal Blue       65  105  225    2.0872   2.3270   2.7081

  White = maximum rapidity on all channels = (2.77, 2.77, 2.77).
  Black = minimum rapidity = (0, 0, 0).
  The BRIGHTNESS of a color is the SUM of channel rapidities.
  This is related to the luminance formula Y = 0.299R + 0.587G + 0.114B
  but in LOG (rapidity) space rather than linear space.

======================================================================
5. MUSICAL TEMPERAMENT AND ARCHITECTURAL PROPORTION
======================================================================

  The Pythagorean comma (12 fifths != 7 octaves) is
  the SAME KIND of incommensurability as the golden ratio
  being irrational (phi != p/q for any integers).

  In architecture: you can't tile a rectangle with golden ratio
  using integer-sided squares (because phi is irrational).
  This is the architectural COMMA.

  In music: you can't stack fifths to get exact octaves
  (because ln(3)/ln(2) is irrational).
  This is the musical COMMA.

  In both cases: the rapidity of the ratio is IRRATIONAL,
  meaning it never lands on the integer rapidity lattice.
  The beauty of both music and architecture comes from
  APPROACHING but never reaching the integer lattice.
  The near-miss IS the beauty.

======================================================================
6. PHOTOGRAPHY AND THE EXPOSURE TRIANGLE
======================================================================

  Photography exposure: E = (f/N)^2 * t * ISO
  where N = f-number, t = shutter speed, ISO = sensitivity.

  The STOP is the unit of exposure: 1 stop = doubling = 1 octave.
  The f-stop series: f/1, f/1.4, f/2, f/2.8, f/4, f/5.6, f/8, ...
  Each step is sqrt(2) = half an octave of f-number.
  (Because light intensity ~ 1/N^2, so 1 stop = N*sqrt(2).)

  In rapidity:
  1 stop of exposure = 1 octave of rapidity.
  The f-stop number has rapidity that increases by ln(2)/4 per stop.
  The ISO has rapidity that increases by ln(2)/2 per stop.
  The shutter speed has rapidity that decreases by ln(2)/2 per stop.

  The exposure triangle IS a rapidity triangle:
  rapidity(aperture) + rapidity(shutter) + rapidity(ISO) = const.

======================================================================
7. FIBONACCI SPIRALS AND THE GOLDEN RAPIDITY
======================================================================

  The Fibonacci spiral: each quarter-turn expands by phi.
  After n quarter-turns: expansion = phi^n.
  rapidity(phi^n) = n * ln(phi)/2 = n * 0.2406.

  After a FULL TURN (4 quarter-turns):
  expansion = phi^4 = phi^3 + phi^2 = 3*phi + 2 = 6.8541
  rapidity = 4 * ln(phi)/2 = 2*ln(phi) = 0.962424
  = 2.7770 octaves

  A full turn of the Fibonacci spiral expands by ~2.77 octaves.
  Compare: an octave of music spans a frequency ratio of 2.
  The Fibonacci spiral is MORE than a doubling per turn.

======================================================================
8. PERCEPTION AND RAPIDITY: STEVENS' POWER LAW
======================================================================

  Stevens' power law: perceived intensity P = k * S^n
  where S = stimulus, n depends on the modality.

  In rapidity: rapidity(P) = n * rapidity(S) + rapidity(k)
  Stevens' law is LINEAR in rapidity space!

  Exponents for different modalities:
  Modality                  Exponent n  rapidity scale
  -------------------------------------------------------
  Brightness                      0.33     compressive
  Loudness                        0.67      sub-linear
  Vibration (finger)              0.95      sub-linear
  Length                          1.00       veridical
  Weight                          1.45       expansive
  Electric shock                  3.50 highly expansive
  Temperature (warmth)            1.60       expansive
  Taste (sweetness)               1.30       expansive

  Brightness (n=0.33): 3 octaves of light = 1 octave of perceived brightness.
  Loudness (n=0.67): 3 octaves of sound = 2 octaves of perceived loudness.
  Electric shock (n=3.5): 1 octave of current = 3.5 octaves of perceived pain!

  Stevens' law in rapidity: P_rapidity = n * S_rapidity + const.
  The exponent n IS the rapidity conversion factor between
  physical stimulus and perceived intensity.

======================================================================
GRAND SUMMARY: BEAUTY IS RAPIDITY NEAR-COMMENSURABILITY
======================================================================

  Beautiful proportions are ratios with SMALL rapidity.
  Perfect symmetry = rapidity 0 (unison).
  Golden ratio = rapidity 0.24 (between major and minor third).
  Octave = rapidity 0.35 (the fundamental doubling).

  BEAUTY arises when rapidities are NEARLY but not exactly
  commensurable. The golden ratio is beautiful because
  it is maximally INCOMMENSURABLE (worst rational approximation).
  It sits at the point of maximum distance from all simple fractions.

  Architecture uses rational approximations to phi (5:8, 3:5).
  Music uses rational approximations to log-ratios (12-TET ~ just).
  Both are TEMPERED versions of irrational rapidity ideals.
  The tempering IS the beauty.
